WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:21.750 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  tessa and i are co-founders of norst  a loungewear label made sustainably by  heritage craft artisans  felicia runs a design studio called  quartus architects  that explores the creation of  experiences within art and architecture  pessa is a community development worker  at an ngo called mercy center working  with the homeless and marginalized  communities  [Music]  design comes alive when it serves a  purpose and addresses real human needs  so we ask  ourselves often what do we each bring to  the table  since both of us are architects by  training it shapes how we see studies  and approach the creative process  an architect draws plants as one seeing  from above  akin to an aerial view but every good  building  is experienced fully from the ground up  and from the inside out  [Music]  the national gallery is a building that  preserves heritage  in a way that is relevant to us today  adaptive reuse by conserving buildings  instead of demolishing them is  sustainable as it reduces carbon  footprint  light filters gently through the  reflective pool  lowering the temperature and creating an  immersive  moment of pause for a space to work well  it must be designed with real people in  mind  people who feel the warmth of sunlight  who hear footsteps on gravel  who grasp the textures of a handrail  space envelops us  similarly we see clothing not as  disposable fashion  but as something we inhabit how can  clothing become a comfortable  second skin that eases our daily  routines  [Music]  from a glance it is easy to write  singapore off as a commercial metropolis  filled with skyscrapers but the gritier  underbelly of shop house alleys  with delicious hawk affair and tables in  chinatown  where uncles play chess late into the  night tell different stories  our studio is located in the chinatown  kyungsik neighborhood  a cultural melting pot of historic shop  houses  and modern buildings five foot ways  reduce the scale of the city  into an intimate passage of rhythmic  arches  they are tailor-made for humans we can  interact with shops  look inside and appreciate the details  we love living in a city of contrast  where multiple diverse perspectives are  woven  into an eclectic tapestry  a lot of my work takes place in arab  street  a place where migrants have become  neighbors and in the case of elbows  carpets  my friends among the colorful carpets  the owners explained the differences  between machine-made  and hand-tuft rugs  it reminds us of the artisan families we  met in indonesia and india  each of them elbow deep in their craft  what really inspires us is seeing people  at work  whether it's a weaver on his step loom  orbitic artisan  applying steaming wax we respect the  dedication that goes into honing a craft  through the generations from grandfather  to father to son  the slow pace of handcrafting reminds us  that design  is a journey enriched by exploration and  seeming detours  it's okay to slow down and find rest  during my free time i like to attend  creative workshops where i learn  something new  the chapter at neil road is a space  where i slow down  and soak in the sights and smells of tea  brewing  having downtime allows me to come back  to the drawing board  with fresh perspectives  the textures of architectural facades  are a constant use  our modular print rope was inspired by  the eye-catching facets  of the concourse tropical facades are  designed  not just for aesthetics but also provide  shade and ventilation  reducing the need for artificial cooling  in fashion we ask the same question how  can we make use of the limited resources  we have to produce  something beautiful that doesn't harm  the earth  many of our artisans come from  agricultural communities  where rivers are often polluted by the  use of toxic dyes  we need to rethink the broken ecosystem  of fashion  like every ecosystem the needs are vast  and competing  we need to sit down and sift through  which values are foremost for us  the home is the main space where these  conversations are fostered  at the table with fellow creatives  nos comes from nostalgia which means a  longing for home  we create pieces that people feel at  home in  wherever they are

